{
  "$description": "TIER 3 - COMPONENT. Mode-INDEPENDENT: written once, referencing Tier 2 only (PRD 5.2 rules 2 and 3). Component CSS consumes these and never reaches past them to Tier 1; tests/contrast/lint-literals.mjs fails the build on a Tier-1 reference outside Tier 2.\n\nThese emit into a `body` rule rather than `:root`. That is not cosmetic. A custom property whose value contains var() is substituted at computed-value time ON THE ELEMENT WHERE IT IS DECLARED - so a Tier-3 property declared on :root, referencing a Tier-2 property that only exists on body[data-jp-theme-light], resolves against nothing and becomes guaranteed-invalid for the whole document. Declaring Tier 3 on `body` puts it in the same scope as Tier 2. See docs/decisions.md D-001.",
