  "splash": {
    "$description": "PRD §8.9 / §6.1. The boot overlay, T3-replaced via ISplashScreen.\n\nREAD THESE VALUES FROM THE DARK PALETTE IN BOTH MODES — `tokensFor(false)`.\nThe splash is the application FRAME at its first frame, and D-007 makes the\nframe dark in both modes; the imported mockup paints it on ink regardless of\nmode too. Taking the current mode's palette would give a white flash before a\ndark chrome in light mode, which is the opposite of what the frame decision is\nfor.\n\nThe consumer applies these as INLINE STYLES rather than CSS, and that is not a\nshortcut: the theme manager is what calls `splash.show(isLight)`, so the splash\npaints while the theme is still loading and `data-jp-theme-name` is not\nreliably set. Every rule gated per D-003 is therefore inert at splash time. The\ntyped token export exists for exactly this class of surface (PRD §7.9).",
    "bg": {
      "$value": "{color.surface.sunken}",
      "$type": "color"
    },
